::Range::
How can you check if a number is within a specified range using the range function?
{
~ Use a loop and check each value in the range.
= Use the in keyword with the range object.
~ Convert the range object to a list and check for inclusion.
~ Use the contains method of the range object.
}

::Range::
Which of the following statements is true about the range function in Python?
{
~ The range function generates a list of numbers immediately.
~ The range function can only be used to generate integers.
= The range function is memory-efficient as it produces numbers on the fly.
~ The range function can only generate positive numbers.
}

::Range::
Which argument is optional when using the range function?
{
~ start
~ stop
= step
~ All arguments are required
}
